# Security headers served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets.
# Lighthouse Best Practices scoring: HSTS + COOP + X-Frame-Options +
# X-Content-Type-Options + Referrer-Policy + Permissions-Policy is the
# set that lifts the score from 96 → 100 on incognito audits.
#
# CSP allows 'unsafe-inline' for scripts because Hero/Cloud/etc. ship
# with `<script is:inline>` blocks (copy buttons, neural canvas,
# waitlist submit). Tightening to nonces is a separate refactor.
#
# Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon hosts (static.cloudflareinsights.com,
# cloudflareinsights.com) are allowlisted in CSP because Cloudflare
# auto-injects the beacon at the zone level — blocking it via CSP
# would create a different console error without fixing the existing
# ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED (which is network-level, environmental).
#
# `connect-src` adds an explicit `https://onebrain.run` token alongside
# `'self'` because Safari/WebKit logs CSP violations for the same-origin
# `/cdn-cgi/rum` RUM endpoint despite `'self'` matching it per spec.
# The explicit hostname suppresses the noise without widening the
# policy meaningfully (it points to the same origin already covered by
# `'self'`). No subdomain wildcards are added — there are no current
# `*.onebrain.run` subdomains and `static.cloudflareinsights.com` is the
# only beacon host in use.
#
# `img-src` is `'self' data:` only — every image on the site is locally
# hosted (`og.jpg`, `brain.svg`, `apple-touch-icon.png`, diagrams), so
# allowing arbitrary `https:` hosts only widens the XSS exfil surface.
# `worker-src 'self'`, `manifest-src 'self'`, and `media-src 'none'`
# are explicit defense-in-depth — `default-src 'self'` already covers
# their fallbacks, but explicit directives prevent a future
# `default-src` relaxation from silently re-opening them.
#
# `challenges.cloudflare.com` is allowlisted in `script-src`,
# `connect-src`, and `frame-src` for Cloudflare Turnstile (anti-spam
# widget on the waitlist form). It loads `/turnstile/v0/api.js`,
# verifies tokens via `POST /turnstile/v0/siteverify` (the call is
# server-side so connect-src is technically belt-and-braces for
# client-side preflight), and renders inside an iframe — hence the
# `frame-src` switch from `'none'` to that single host.
#
# HSTS `preload` (added 2026-05-19) is a one-way commitment: once
# submitted to hstspreload.org, onebrain.run + every `*.onebrain.run`
# subdomain is locked to HTTPS in browsers for ~max-age (2y). Rollback =
# drop the directive here, ship the update for max-age duration, then
# request removal at hstspreload.org/removal. Any future subdomain
# (e.g. Cloud's `app.onebrain.run`) MUST launch HTTPS-only from day 1.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://onebrain.run https://cloudflareinsights.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; media-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/diagrams/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/brain.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/og.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
